        ) VALUES (
            'c07c6348-37d0-4e87-9339-cfb4876868a3', 'SSC CGL 2025 Tier I Shift 2', 2025, 'Shift 2', 'English Comprehension', 95,
            'Find the part of the sentence that contains an error: 
That the policy omits provisions for backward compatibility (1) / is less troubling than the belief (2) / that all regional 
bodies will, without any pressure, (3) / complies with the central directive as issued (4). 
(a) (1) 
(b) (2) 
(c) (3) 
(d) (4) 
Ans.(d) 
 
Q96. Identify the misspelt word: 
(a) Perseverance 
(b) Supersede 
(c) Privillage 
(d) Mischievous 
Ans.(c) 
 
Q97. Select the sentence containing the homonym of the highlighted word: 
The prince’s gules stood out clearly on the family coat of arms. 
(a) The shield displayed gules and argent in bold patterns. 
(b) The cook served a dish with a sauce of rich gules and cumin. 
(c) The gules trim on the banner represented a warrior tradition. 
(d) The guide described the meaning of gules to the audience. 
Ans.(b) 
 
Q98. Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence: 
The teacher asked to the student to submit the papers. 
(a) asked the student that submit the papers 
(b) requested the student to submit papers 
(c) asked the student to submit the papers 
(d) told to the student submit papers 
Ans.(c) 
 
Q99. Choose the correct meaning of idiom: Leave no stone unturned 
(a) To keep shifting from one place to another repeatedly 
(b) To make every possible effort to achieve a goal 
(c) To remain quiet as a form of protest 
(d) To obey someone without questioning 
Ans.(b) 
 
Q100. Rearrange the following sentences to form a coherent paragraph: 
1. One effective approach is to broaden energy options by moving away from fossil fuels towards renewables such as 
solar, wind, and geothermal energy. 
2. To reduce the severe impacts of climate change, nations must sharply cut dependence on high-carbon energy 
generation. 
3. This transition not only lowers greenhouse gas output but also improves air quality and opens up new economic 
possibilities. 
4. In addition, measures that encourage energy efficiency in buildings and transport can further reduce total energy 
use.', '/question-images/SSC_CGL_12_Sep_2025_S2_English_p20_q95_0.png', '2, 1, 3, 4', '1, 2, 4, 3',
            '3, 1, 4, 2', '2, 3, 1, 4 
Ans.(a)', NULL, NULL,
            2.0, 0.5, 'SSC-CGL-12-Sep-2025-S2-English.pdf', 'failed_validation', '["MISSING_CORRECT_ANSWER: Official correct answer option is missing or invalid."]'::jsonb
