            'a5f55d19-91bf-43b4-bbb0-87750a3a5185', 'SSC CGL 2023 Tier I Shift 1 (2023-03-06)', 2023, 'Shift 1', 'General Intelligence & Reasoning', 33,
            'In this question, a question is followed by two statements numbered (I) and (II). You have to decide whether the data provided in the \\frac{statement}{s} are sufficient to answer the question. Read both the statements and choose your answer carefully. Question: P, Q, R, S, T, U and V are 7 people standing in a row all facing North (not necessarily in the same order). Who is standing second to the right of T? Statements: (I) U is standing 3 rd from the right end and 2 nd to the left of R. (II) Q is standing to the immediate right of T. Q is standing 2 nd to the left of P.', '/question-images/SSC_CGL_6_March_2023_p14_q33_4.png', 'The data in both the Statements (I) and (II) together are sufficient to answer the', 'The data in Statement (II) alone is sufficient to answer the question, while the data in',
