        ) VALUES (
            'eb305f0c-3102-4e44-a517-27a8b7b14e26', 'SSC CGL 2025 Tier I Shift 3', 2025, 'Shift 3', 'Quantitative Aptitude', 57,
            'The radius of a circular plate is increased by 8%. What will be the approximate percentage increase in its area? 
(a) 8% 
(b) 15% 
(c) 16.64% 
(d) 17.28% 
Ans.(c) 
 
Q58. A rectangular prism has a base area of 36 cm². If its height is increased by 25% from the original height of 12 cm, 
what is the new volume? 
(a) 432 cm³ 
(b) 486 cm³ 
(c) 504 cm³ 
(d) 540 cm³ 
Ans.(d) 
 
Q59. A solid metal sphere of radius 6 cm is completely immersed in a vertical cylindrical vessel containing water, causing 
the water level to rise by 4 cm. What is the radius of the cylinder? 
(a) 4√2 cm 
(b) 5√2 cm 
(c) 6√2 cm 
(d) 8√2 cm 
Ans.(c) 
 
Q60. A train covers 1.2 km in 1 minute. How far will it travel in 2 hours 15 minutes? 
(a) 162 km 
(b) 156 km 
(c) 171 km 
(d) 168 km 
Ans.(a) 
 
Q61. Two farmers, X and Y, hire a field. X keeps 18 oxen there for 5 months and 20 goats for 3 months. Y keeps 24 goats 
for 7 months and 30 sheep for 6 months. If 2 oxen eat as much as 5 goats, and 3 goats eat as much as 4 sheep, what 
fraction of the total rent should X pay? 
(a) \\frac{90}{196} 
(b) \\frac{95}{196} 
(c) \\frac{10}{196} 
(d) \\frac{111}{196} 
Ans.(b) 
 
Q62. Three batches of students have average ages 17, 19, and 23 years respectively. If their numbers are in the ratio 3 
: 4 : 6, what is the overall average age of all the students? 
(a) 19.41 
(b) 20.38 
(c) 21.20 
(d) 18.9 
Ans.(b)', '/question-images/SSC_CGL_Held_on_12_Sep_2025_S3_p11_q57_0.png', NULL, NULL,
