        ) VALUES (
            'f9f8161b-f019-479f-aa88-a1a51f5c75bb', 'SSC CGL 2025 Tier I Shift 3', 2025, 'Shift 3', 'Quantitative Aptitude', 69,
            'C and D invested ₹1,40,000 and ₹1,80,000, respectively. C remained for 9 months and D for 8 months. If C''s share 
in the profit is ₹18,900, what is the total profit? 
(a) ₹40,500 
(b) ₹36,000 
(c) ₹34,200 
(d) ₹38,400 
Ans.(a) 
 
Q70. A television set is sold for ₹Q and the shopkeeper earns a profit of 25%. During a clearance sale, he marks the 
same set at 1.4Q and allows a discount of 15% on the marked price. What is his profit percentage during the sale? 
(a) 45.75% 
(b) 40% 
(c) 48.75% 
(d) 50% 
Ans.(c) 
 
Q71. A trader marks his goods 30% above the cost price and then allows a discount of 12%. What is his profit 
percentage? 
(a) 14.4% 
(b) 15.6% 
(c) 16.5% 
(d) 18.0% 
Ans.(a) 
 
Q72. A shopkeeper marks his products 50% above the cost price and allows a discount of 20% on the marked price. He 
also gives an additional cash discount of ₹120 and still makes a profit of 16% on cost. What is the cost price of the 
product? 
(a) ₹1,800 
(b) ₹3,000 
(c) ₹2,200 
(d) ₹2,400 
Ans.(b) 
 
Q73. X lent ₹6,000 to Y for 3 years and ₹4,000 to Z for 2 years, both at the same simple interest rate. In total, he 
received ₹2,000 as interest from both. What is the rate of interest per annum(nearest integer)? 
(a) 8% 
(b) 10% 
(c) 12% 
(d) 15% 
Ans.(a) 
 
Q74. A sector of a circle has a central angle of 150^\\circ and radius 10 cm. Another sector of the same circle has a central 
angle of 5π/6 radians. What is the ratio of the area of the first sector to that of the second? 
(a) 3 : 4 
(b) 1 : 1 
(c) 4 : 5 
(d) 5 : 6', '/question-images/SSC_CGL_Held_on_12_Sep_2025_S3_p13_q69_0.png', '“Due dates must be met strictly,” said the manager.', '“You should meet the due dates strictly,” said the manager.',
            '4-3-1-2', '4-1-3-2 
Ans.(d) 
 
