Q81. A sentence is provided in direct speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys 
the sentence in its corresponding indirect speech: 
She said, “Finish it right now.” 
(a) She said to finish it instantly. 
(b) She told to finish it then. 
(c) She told me to finish it immediately. 
(d) She told me finish it right now. 
Ans.(c) 
 
Q82. Select the correct option: 
The committee issued several directives, none of _______ were implemented. 
(a) that 
(b) them 
(c) which 
(d) whom 
Ans.(c) 
 
Q83. A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately 
conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech: 
The manager remarked that employees needed to submit their reports by Monday. 
(a) “Employees need to submit their reports by Monday,” the manager remarked. 
(b) “Employees needed to submit their reports by Monday,” the manager said. 
(c) “Submit your reports by Monday,” the manager ordered. 
(d) “You were to submit your reports by Monday,” the manager said. 
Ans.(a) 
 
Q84. Select the correct option: 
Her interpretation was diametrically ________ to the accepted doctrine. 
(a) adverse 
(b) averse 
(c) inverse 
(d) opposed 
Ans.(d) 
 
