            'Two individuals, P and Q, rent a field together. P has 20 oxen grazed for 5 months. Q grazes 30 buffalo for 5 months 
and 40 sheep for 3 months. Relationships: 2 oxen = 5 buffalo, 3 buffalo = 6 sheep. What fraction of rent should P pay? 
(a) \\frac{15}{46} 
(b) \\frac{25}{46} 
(c) \\frac{33}{47} 
(d) \\frac{19}{23} 
Ans.(b) 
 
Q57. P, Q, and R started a business with capitals in ratio 1:2:4. After 4 months, R withdrew 50% of his capital. After 
another 2 months, Q withdrew 25% of his capital. The business continued for 12 months total. Total profit is ₹2,40,000. 
Find profit ratio P : Q : R. 
(a) 32 : 21 : 12 
(b) 21 : 12 : 33 
(c) 12 : 21 : 32 
(d) 12 : 33 : 42 
Ans.(c) 
 
Q58. The average age of 30 students in a class is 15 years. When a new student is admitted, the average increases by 
