m, find its height. 
(a) 10 m 
(b) 12 m', '/question-images/SSC_CGL_T_I_Similar_Paper_Held_p13_q69_0.png', '______. Such spatial remnants resist the antiseptic linearity of redevelopment blueprints, proposing instead a fugitive 
temporality-discordant, accreted, and refractory. Within this interpretive frame, the ruin ceases to be a lapse in 
engineering; it becomes an overcoded lexicon of disintegration. Its idiom reverberates through fractured masonry and 
derelict signage, repudiating the veneer of municipal optimism. To aestheticize such degradation uncritically is to 
engage in epistemic', '______—where dispossession is stylized and precarity rendered picturesque. What parades as 
revitalization frequently entails spatial excision, evacuating memory in deference to speculative capital while 
"preservation" morphs into curated sterilization. To approach ruins hermeneutically is to substitute instrumentality 
with',
            '______—to permit debris to articulate what masterplans efface. These terrains solicit not embellishment but 
critical excavation, wherein rusted girders and dormant corridors metamorphose into loci of semantic dissent. Yet', 'Ephemiral 
Ans.(b) 
 
