            'In this question, two statements I and II have been given. These statements may be independent causes or effects of independent causes or a common cause. One of the statements may be the effect of the other statement. Read both statements and select the correct answer. I. Country X reduced their crude oil import by 6% in the last 5 years. II. The automobile industry in Country X has witnessed a sharp decline of 13% in its growth margin this year.', '/question-images/SSC_CGL_2022_Tier_II_Official__p21_q47_0.png', 'Both I and II are effects of independent causes.', 'I is the cause and II is its possible effect.',
