            'bdb205a7-2bb9-4e52-8247-e97cffd6bf04', 'SSC CGL 2022 Tier II Shift 1 (2023-03-03)', 2022, 'Shift 1', 'General Intelligence & Reasoning', 50,
            'Given below is a question followed by two statements I and II. Read both statements carefully to decide which one of them is sufficient to answer the question. Six people - A, B, C, D, E and F are sitting in a straight line facing north. Who sits to the immediate left of D? (I) A sits second from one of the extreme ends of the line. Only two people sit between A and B. E sits to the immediate right of C. (II) C sits third from the left end of the line. Only one person sits between C and F. E sits third to the right of F.', '/question-images/SSC_CGL_2022_Tier_II_Official__p22_q50_1.png', 'Data in statement II alone is sufficient to answer the question while data in statement', 'Data in statement I alone is sufficient to answer the question while data in statement',
